//! Differential test: every selector in the corpus must select the same node
//! set here as `the reference implementation` (`Selector(html).css(sel)`) selects in
//! Python, on every page of the corpus.
//!
//! `testdata/css_golden.jsonl` holds one row per query — **343 selectors x 10
//! HTML pages, plus 729 rows evaluated from a non-root context node: 4159 rows
//! and 10 134 result entries** — generated by running the reference
//! implementation. The pages live in `testdata/pages/` so both sides parse
//! byte-identical input.
//!
//! # What is covered
//!
//! Type / universal / class / id selectors, every attribute operator
//! (`= ^= $= *= ~= |= !=`, plus presence and empty operands), all four
//! combinators, comma groups, every `:nth-child(an+b)` spelling,
//! `:nth-of-type`, `:nth-last-*`, `:first`/`:last`/`:only-child`,
//! `:only-of-type`, `:empty`, `:root`, `:scope`, `:not()`, `:has()`, `:is()`,
//! the HTML state pseudo-classes, `:lang()`, `:contains()`, `::text`,
//! `::attr()`, escaped identifiers (`#a\.b`, `#\31 23start`), namespace
//! prefixes (`|div`, `*|div`, `[*|lang]`), ASCII-case questions on names,
//! classes, ids and attribute values — and **thirty invalid selectors**, whose
//! Python exception text is recorded so the port is checked for rejecting what
//! the reference rejects, not just for accepting what it accepts.
//!
//! The pages are `shop` (well-formed), `tables` (nested tables, an implied
//! `<tbody>`), `malformed` (unclosed tags, misnesting, duplicate ids, bare
//! attributes), `svg` (inline SVG + MathML), `unicode` (Cyrillic / CJK / RTL /
//! emoji / entities), `forms` (every form-control state), `blog` (deep
//! nesting, sibling runs, comments), `quirks` (no doctype, upper-case tags,
//! attributes and values), `edge` (whitespace-only and comment-only elements,
//! escaped identifiers, entity-laden attribute values, tab/newline class
//! separators) and `weird` (`<template>`, `<noscript>`, `<iframe>`,
//! `xlink:href`, `<foreignObject>`, MathML).
//!
//! The scoped rows are `Selector(html).css(ctx)[0].css(sel)` — three context
//! nodes per page — and pin lxml's `descendant-or-self::` scoping, which is
//! neither `querySelectorAll` nor a subtree query.
//!
//! # Regenerating
//!
//! The generator lives outside the repository because it needs the reference
//! interpreter:
//!
//! ```text
//! $JOB/tmp/pyref/bin/python $JOB/tmp/u5v/gen_css_golden.py
//! ```
//!
//! (`u5v/pages_extra.py` + `gen/pages.py` hold the HTML, `u5v/sel_extra.py` +
//! `u5v/sel_scoped.py` + `gen/selectors_corpus.py` the selectors; the script
//! writes both `testdata/pages/*.html` and the `.jsonl`.)
//!
//! # Identity, not serialisation
//!
//! Result entries are compared on *node identity* — tag name, the full sorted
//! attribute set, and the element's whitespace-stripped string value — rather
//! than on raw outer HTML, because html5ever and libxml2 legitimately spell the
//! same tree differently (attribute quoting, void-element syntax, entity
//! re-escaping). The generator still records `html` and lxml's `getpath()` for
//! every element; the path is additionally asserted for pages whose tree shape
//! the two parsers agree on (`shape_stable`).
//!
//! # Divergences
//!
//! Rows that cannot match are listed in [`EXPECTED_DIVERGENCES`] and
//! [`EXPECTED_DIVERGENT_SELECTORS`] with the reason, and are asserted to *keep*
//! diverging — never silently skipped. The table is also checked for
//! staleness: an entry that starts passing fails the test.
//!
//! **3948 of 4159 rows reproduce the reference implementation exactly.** The
//! 211 that do not are 70 selectors the CSS Selectors 4 grammar accepts and
//! cssselect rejects (7 selectors x 10 pages), 119 rows of html5ever-vs-libxml2
//! *tree shape* (implied `<tbody>`, a synthesised `<head>`, the adoption
//! agency), 9 rows of `browser-dom`'s stricter `remove_blank_text`, 8 rows of
//! the lxml scoping quirk `API.md` deviation 6 describes, and 5 rows of
//! minimised boolean attributes and SVG attribute-name case. None is a CSS matching bug — see [`EXPECTED_DIVERGENCES`] for how
//! that claim is checked rather than asserted.

use std::collections::BTreeSet;

use browser_dom::{Document, NodeRef, ParseOptions};
use browser_selectors::matching::{Match, MatchValue, TextRole};
use browser_selectors::parse::parse_selector;
use serde_json::Value;

